+[Term]
+id: GO:7770074
+name: protein O-linked glycosylation via N-acetylglucosamine
+namespace: biological_process
+def: "A glycoprotein biosynthetic process starting with the covalent linkage of a single N-acetylglucosamine via a beta-glycosidic bond to the oxygen atom of a serine or threonine side chain in a protein, resulting in the formation of a protein O-linked glycan. In contrast to other forms of protein O-linked glycosylation, the sugar is not further elongated into a larger oligosaccharide chain." [PMID:35536957]
